Notes for this system's distribution of gcc-2.95.3:

1.  This is GNU GCC 2.95.3 as GNU released it, with the changes
    NetBSD 1.6 made to it, which carried it as "2.95.3 (NetBSD nb3)",
    and this system added to it as i386-unknown-bsd4.4elf
    (docs/provenance/imports.md, *The toolchain*).  Its C and C++
    compilers are built, as gcc-2.3.3's were, and its C++ library,
    libstdc++ 2.10.0 with libio; not its Objective C, Fortran, CHILL
    or Java.

2.  It is built twice.  build/sysroot.sh builds it on the machine
    doing a cross build, to make programs for this system; and
    `make' here, which `make build' runs, builds it to run on this
    system itself, the i386, from 'makefile', which configures GNU's
    sources and runs GNU's own Makefiles, as contrib/gcc-2.3.3's and
    contrib/binutils-2.11.2's makefiles do.  It builds in a directory
    of its own, the object directory when the build has one, and
    obj.${MACHINE} here when not.

3.  `make install' puts it where 4.4BSD put its GCC, under
    /usr/libexec/gcc2: the driver as gcc-2.95.3 and
    gcc-i386-unknown-bsd4.4elf, the preprocessor as cpp, which
    /usr/bin/cpp runs, and cc1, cpp0, collect2, libgcc.a and GCC's
    headers in gcc-lib/i386-unknown-bsd4.4elf/2.95.3.  /usr/bin/gcc
    is a symbolic link to the driver, and /usr/bin/cc to gcc.  The
    pages, formatted, go in /usr/contrib/man/cat1.

4.  And C++ where gcc-2.3.3 put it: cc1plus beside cc1; the g++
    driver as g++-2.95.3, with c++-2.95.3 linked to it, where
    gcc-2.3.3 installed g++-2.3.3 and c++-2.3.3; /usr/bin/g++ a
    symbolic link to it and /usr/bin/c++ to g++; libstdc++.a beside
    libgcc.a, which the driver searches; and the C++ headers --
    libstdc++'s, libio's and _G_config.h -- in
    /usr/libexec/gcc2/g++-include, where gcc-2.3.3 looked for them.
    libgcc holds C++'s own support, new, delete, exceptions and type
    information, which is all groff, the system's nroff, needs of
    C++'s libraries: it is linked by gcc, as Berkeley configured it.

Therefore to build and install it on this system simply type:

% make
% make install
